    "markingSupplements": {
      "22ci": "Readable calculation: Each bolt carries 30,000 / 3 = 10,000 N. Single-shear area = π × 16² / 4 = 201.1 mm². Shear stress = 49.7 N/mm² = 49.7 MPa. Credit relevant working for partial marks.",
      "22cii": "Readable calculation: allowable stress = 250 / 2.5 = 100 MPa. Actual shear stress is 49.7 MPa, below the allowable value, so the bolts are safe. Alternatively actual factor of safety = 250 / 49.7 ≈ 5.03, exceeding 2.5.",
      "23ci": "Readable sample calculation: cable tension T = 12,000 × sin(51.8°) / sin(78.2°) = 9,633.87 N (about 9.63 kN). Accept equivalent force-equilibrium or scaled graphical solutions and reasonable rounding.",
      "23cii": "Readable sample calculation: mechanical advantage = 12,000 / 9,633.87 = 1.2456. Efficiency = MA / VR × 100 = 1.2456 / 2 × 100 = 62.3%. Allow correct follow-through using the student’s earlier cable force when the method is valid.",
      "26c": "Transcription of the graphical sample solution: the truss has a 9 kN downward load and a 15 kN load at 60° to the horizontal, span 2800 mm, height 700 mm and half-span 1400 mm. θ = atan(700/1400) = 26.565°. Taking moments about A: R_B = (9×1.4 + 15sin60°×2.8 − 15cos60°×0.7)/2.8 = 15.615 kN upward. On the right side of a section through member M, vertical equilibrium gives F_M sinθ = 15.615 − 15sin60° = 2.625 kN. F_M = 5.8697 kN = 5869.7 N, in tension. These are equivalent units; accept sensible rounding and alternative valid methods. The final line of the printed sample has an inconsistent unit rendering; use 5.8697 kN or 5869.7 N."
    },
